  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Lead sulphate-white</p><p>Lead sulphate is a white, somewhat crystalline, very heavy powder, its specific gravity being about <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. It is only slightly soluble in water, insoluble in dilute acids and alcohol, but soluble in solutions of ammonium salts and strong sulphuric acid.</p><p>Ammonium sulphide-soluble</p><p>Lead iodide-bright yellow</p><p>Ammonium arsinomolybdate-yellow</p><p>Hence, the answer is option B.</p>",
    "image": null
